<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <base href="/" />
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    @* No static <title> here: every page supplies its own through <PageTitle>, and with
       prerendering the HeadOutlet emits a real <title> element into this head. A second,
       earlier one would win in the served HTML (browsers and crawlers take the first). *@
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    @* No static description here either, for the same reason as the title above: every page emits
       its own through PageHeader's lead, and an earlier one in the served HTML would win. *@
    <link rel="icon" href="favicon.ico" type="image/x-icon" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/app.css" />
    @* Same render mode as the app itself, so <PageTitle> keeps working after hydration. *@
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="InteractiveWebAssembly" />
</head>

<body>
    @* Prerendered on the server, then hydrated by the WebAssembly runtime. Pages only touch
       the browser from OnAfterRenderAsync and event handlers, which never run during the
       prerender pass - see Layout/MainLayout.razor for the RendererInfo-driven hydration hint. *@
    <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveWebAssembly" />

    <div id="blazor-error-ui">
        An unhandled error has occurred.
        <a href="." class="reload">Reload</a>
        <span class="dismiss">🗙</span>
    </div>

    @* Loaded before the Blazor script so window.BitButil exists by the time the app boots. *@
    <script src="_content/Bit.Butil/bit-butil.js"></script>
    <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
</body>

</html>
